Build the analog joystick port (hw/input/gameport.c, overlaid from
gamepad/qemu/ by scripts/prepare-qemu.sh). M13 path B,
docs/tracks/m13-gamepads.md.

QEMU has never answered 0x201: nothing in hw/ models the gameport, and
sb16.c is the DSP and mixer only — the port that sits at 0x200-0x207 on a
real Sound Blaster is not in it. A DOS game reads that port itself and has
no other way to find a joystick, so DOS had no path to a controller at all
before this; path A's USB HID gamepad needs a USB stack DOS has not got.

Its own Kconfig symbol rather than riding a sound card's: the family's
card is a separate choice (bundle::Sound, doc 20) and a joystick should
not appear and vanish with it. `default y / depends on ISA_BUS` is
exactly "this machine has an ISA bus", which is the only condition the
port has — the same shape patch 26 uses with CONFIG_USB_HID.

The host side drives it through gameport_set_state() (gamepad/qemu/
gameport.h), called from the embed shim's input bottom half under the BQL
with the same four axis bytes, hat and button bitmap the usb-gamepad
takes, so one call feeds whichever of the two devices the machine has.

diff --git a/hw/input/Kconfig b/hw/input/Kconfig
index a116cb82df..2a0f3fdaf3 100644
--- a/hw/input/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/input/Kconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,14 @@
 config ADB
     bool
 
+# win98-xp-virt: the analog joystick port at 0x200-0x207 (M13 path B,
+# docs/tracks/m13-gamepads.md). Overlaid into hw/input/ by
+# scripts/prepare-qemu.sh; the only condition is an ISA bus to sit on.
+config GAMEPORT
+    bool
+    default y
+    depends on ISA_BUS
+
 config PCKBD
     bool
     select PS2
diff --git a/hw/input/meson.build b/hw/input/meson.build
index 90a214962c..df6959cedf 100644
--- a/hw/input/meson.build
+++ b/hw/input/meson.build
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 system_ss.add(files('hid.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_ADB', if_true: files('adb.c', 'adb-mouse.c', 'adb-kbd.c'))
+system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_GAMEPORT', if_true: files('gameport.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PCKBD', if_true: files('pckbd.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PL050', if_true: files('pl050.c'))
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_PS2', if_true: files('ps2.c'))
